{
  "summary": "Adds an `auto_outbound_mode` setting to the functional test framework and introduces a new test script `p2p_outbound_management.py`. In this mode, the node under test is allowed to autonomously initiate outbound connections to addresses in addrman via a SOCKS5 proxy that redirects them to Python P2P peers or other test nodes. The PR also refactors `p2p_private_broadcast.py` to use the shared test framework implementation instead of its own custom proxy redirect logic.",
  "problem": "P2P logic where bitcoind autonomously chooses when and where to initiate outbound connections has historically lacked functional test coverage because standard tests establish connections inward or use manual `add_outbound_p2p_connection` calls. Important outbound connection management behaviors—such as opening an extra connection on a stale tip, periodic block-relay-only peer rotation, and network diversification—could not be easily tested end-to-end.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description notes that auto_outbound_mode 'allows to test the code in which the node decides to make connections - in contrast to the existing add_outbound_p2p_connection where the functional test initiates the connections.'",
    "Adds functional test coverage for previously uncovered or under-tested outbound P2P mechanisms merged across multiple past PRs: stale tip extra connection (#11560), periodic block-relay-only connections (#19858), and network diversification (#27213)."
  ],
