  "changed_since_previous": "Diff provided matches the scope of the previous description; no structural changes to the commits or implementation approach.",
  "card": "Adds an auto_outbound_mode helper to the functional test framework and introduces functional test coverage for automatic outbound connection management. Functional tests typically rely on the test runner manually initiating connections, leaving the node's autonomous outbound connection decisions untested in an end-to-end environment. By routing autonomous addrman connections through a SOCKS5 proxy back to controllable Python P2P test peers, this PR exercises stale-tip extra connection logic, scheduled block-relay-only peer probing, and network diversification across IPv4, Tor, and CJDNS. It also dedupes test proxy logic previously isolated inside p2p_private_broadcast.py.",
